##########################################################################
# DatabaseChangePackage-5Stage - BuildMaster OtterScript Plan (thin-runner shape)
#
# !! EDITING THIS FILE IS NOT ENOUGH - SYNC IT TO THE RAFT !!
#   BuildMaster executes the copy of this plan stored in its raft, NOT this
#   file. Committing a change here does nothing until you run:
#       Sync-BuildMasterPlans -Path <thisFile>
#   The paired stage runner (Invoke-DatabasePackageBuildMasterStage.ps1) IS
#   read from disk at run time, so a commit that changes both leaves the raft
#   passing the OLD argument list to the NEW parameter block. When the missing
#   argument is a [Parameter(Mandatory)] one, PowerShell prompts a console that
#   nobody can answer and the stage HANGS FOREVER with no error - build stuck
#   'active', log ending at "Executing pwsh...", near-zero CPU, and no
#   _generated/buildmaster/<BuildMasterBuildId>/ directory.
#   This cost a release cycle on 2026-08-03 in the PowerShellModule pipeline.
#   Root cause, triage checklist, and fail-fast guidance:
#       SolutionDocumentation/BuildMaster-Plan-Raft-Sync-Requirement.md
#
# Variables (Application Variables - set in BuildMaster Application config):
#   $ApplicationName    - BuildMaster application name, e.g. "ATAPUtilitiesDatabase"
#   $DatabaseApplication - Source application name used to locate
#                         Database/<DatabaseApplication>/, e.g. "ATAPUtilities"
#   $DatabaseStream     - Optional stream name; empty for single-stream.
#                         Resolves package id <App>.Database vs
#                         <App>.<Stream>.Database.
#   $ExcludedMigrationFileNames
#                       - Optional semicolon-delimited list of exact SQL file
#                         names to exclude from package creation. The runner
#                         rejects paths and duplicate names, passes the list to
#                         New-DatabaseChangePackage, and records it in the
#                         immutable build context.
#   $Branch             - source branch name supplied by monitor/poller
#   $SourcePath         - absolute path to the developer/build worktree
#   $ProGetBaseUrl      - Base URL of the ProGet server hosting the feeds
#   ProGet API key      - Arguments carry only ProGet.BuildMaster.API.Key as a
#                         SecretName; no environment fallback is permitted.
#   BuildMaster stage   - passed explicitly from $PipelineStageName so
#                         deployment targets do not depend on agent env vars
#   $BuildMasterBuildId - runtime value from $BuildMasterId(build), used to
#                         isolate generated inter-stage state under
#                         _generated/buildmaster/<BuildMasterBuildId>/.
#   Per-tier DB connection-string secret names (required Application Variables):
#     $ExperimentalDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName
#     $DevelopmentDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName
#     $IntegrationDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName
#     $QADatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName
#     $ProductionDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName
#                         Bitwarden item names (NOT values) for each tier's
#                         database connection string (see SprintInfrastructure-
#                         Naming.md §4). The runner fails before publish or
#                         promotion when the current tier's name is absent,
#                         enforces a Flyway rehearsal before promoting into that
#                         tier, and applies (migrate) the package to that tier's
#                         database afterward. The runner resolves the
#                         secret value from Bitwarden by name; values never
#                         appear in Arguments.
#
# Five stages map to five canonical database feeds:
#   Experimental -> database-experimental (build .nupkg + publish)
#   Development  -> database-development  (promote)
#   Integration  -> database-integration  (promote)
#   QA           -> database-qa           (promote)
#   Production   -> database-stable       (promote)
#
# Immutable build strategy:
#   Adheres to the immutable build strategy: the package is produced only in
#   the Experimental stage by New-DatabaseChangePackage; later stages promote
#   that same immutable .nupkg via Promote-DatabaseChangePackage. The
#   version.json prerelease label is interpreted as a promotion ceiling.
#   See SolutionDocumentation/Immutable-Build-Strategy.md and
#   SolutionDocumentation/Database-Package-Artifact-And-Feed-Decision.md.
#
# Per-tier database apply + rehearsal:
#   Promotion alone only moves the immutable .nupkg between feeds. For every
#   tier, the runner:
#     - (non-Experimental) runs a Flyway rehearsal BEFORE promotion and blocks
#       the promotion if the rehearsal fails (rehearsal-before-promotion is
#       enforced in code, not just documented), and
#     - applies (Flyway migrate) the package to that tier's database AFTER
#       the stage's promotion/publish, taking a pre-migration snapshot for the
#       permanent Integration/QA/Production tiers.
#   A stage cannot complete when its connection secret is absent or apply is
#   bypassed. The completion marker is written only after a successful apply.
#   See SolutionDocumentation/Database-Change-Unit-and-Flyway-Promotion.md §5/§17.
#
# This plan is assigned as a per-stage deployment step in the BuildMaster UI.
# Keep the OtterScript surface tiny; the PowerShell runner owns stage/context
# branching, ceiling-clamp enforcement, per-tier completion markers, run-
# context JSON, secret-safe ProGet publish/promote invocations, and the
# per-tier Flyway rehearsal + apply.
##########################################################################

# BuildTooling module used by every stage command.
set $BuildToolingModuleManifest = $PathCombine($SourcePath, src\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.PowerShell.psd1);
set $BuildMasterPlanScriptDir = $PathCombine($SourcePath, src\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.BuildMaster\Plans);
set $InvokeDatabasePackageStageScript = $PathCombine($BuildMasterPlanScriptDir, Invoke-DatabasePackageBuildMasterStage.ps1);

set $BuildMasterBuildId = $BuildMasterId(build);
set $BuildMasterBuildNumber = $BuildNumber;
set $BuildMasterExecutionId = $ExecutionId;

Exec
(
    FileName: pwsh,
    Arguments: >>-NoProfile -File "$InvokeDatabasePackageStageScript" -BuildToolingModulePath "$BuildToolingModuleManifest" -SourcePath "$SourcePath" -BuildMasterBuildId "$BuildMasterBuildId" -BuildNumber "$BuildMasterBuildNumber" -ExecutionId "$BuildMasterExecutionId" -ApplicationName "$ApplicationName" -DatabaseApplication "$DatabaseApplication" -DatabaseStream "$DatabaseStream" -ExcludedMigrationFileNames "$ExcludedMigrationFileNames" -Branch "$Branch" -Stage "$PipelineStageName" -ProGetUrl "$ProGetBaseUrl" -ProGetApiKeySecretName "$ProGetApiKeySecretName" -ExperimentalDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName "$ExperimentalDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName" -DevelopmentDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName "$DevelopmentDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName" -IntegrationDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName "$IntegrationDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName" -QADatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName "$QADatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName" -ProductionDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName "$ProductionDatabaseDBConnectionStringSecretName">>,
    WorkingDirectory: $SourcePath,
    SuccessExitCode: 0
);
